WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.493 --> 00:00:22.177
As the next day began to dawn, Sister Simplice was busy preparing some medicine for Fantine.

2
00:00:23.138 --> 00:00:26.841
Suddenly she looked up and saw Mayor Madeleine standing in front of her.

3
00:00:27.681 --> 00:00:31.624
His first task upon arriving home had been to send a letter to his banker.

4
00:00:32.136 --> 00:00:34.478
Then he had come immediately to the infirmary.

5
00:00:34.498 --> 00:00:36.979
"Oh, you startled me!"

6
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.620
said Sister Simplice.

7
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:44.284
"And something terrible must have happened to you because your hair has turned completely white!"

8
00:00:45.265 --> 00:00:46.346
"What are you talking about?"

9
00:00:47.106 --> 00:00:51.049
Sister Simplice found a mirror and showed the mayor his reflection.

10
00:00:51.069 --> 00:00:53.871
"Imagine that," he said quietly.

11
00:00:53.891 --> 00:00:55.311
"How's Fantine?"

12
00:00:56.232 --> 00:01:01.936
Sister Simplice explained that Fantine had improved because she believed that he had gone to fetch Cosette.

13
00:01:03.248 --> 00:01:06.349
Somehow the nun knew that he hadn't been to Montfermeil.

14
00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.291
"What will we tell her when she realizes Cosette is not here?"

15
00:01:10.711 --> 00:01:11.872
asked Sister Simplice.

16
00:01:11.892 --> 00:01:13.913
"It would be wrong to lie to her.

17
00:01:14.513 --> 00:01:15.993
Are you going to get Cosette soon?"

18
00:01:16.014 --> 00:01:18.615
"Of course, but it'll take some time.

19
00:01:19.275 --> 00:01:20.515
May I see Fantine now?"

20
00:01:21.176 --> 00:01:23.997
The sick young woman opened her eyes when the mayor entered.

21
00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:27.038
"Where is Cosette?"

22
00:01:27.498 --> 00:01:31.020
she asked, radiating happiness as she said her daughter's name.

23
00:01:31.812 --> 00:01:33.614
Just then the doctor entered the room.

24
00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:36.696
"Stay calm, my dear," said the doctor.

25
00:01:36.716 --> 00:01:40.660
"Your child is here, but you cannot see her until you're cured.

26
00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:43.843
The excitement of seeing her will make your illness worse."

27
00:01:44.903 --> 00:01:45.584
"I'm well!"

28
00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:48.106
insisted Fantine, trying to sit up.

29
00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:51.149
She fell back, coughing against her pillow.

30
00:01:51.169 --> 00:01:55.553
"But perhaps you're right."

31
00:01:56.513 --> 00:02:02.121
After the doctor and Sister Simplice left the room, the mayor sat by her bed, holding her hand.

32
00:02:02.141 --> 00:02:06.662
"Montfermeil is such a pretty place, isn't it, Mayor Madeleine?

33
00:02:07.762 --> 00:02:09.503
And what did you think of the Thenardiers?"

34
00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:15.284
The mayor looked anxiously at Fantine, but before he could say anything, she cried out.

35
00:02:15.304 --> 00:02:17.105
"I hear my darling singing!"

36
00:02:17.965 --> 00:02:21.286
A child was playing in the courtyard, the daughter of a servant.

37
00:02:21.866 --> 00:02:24.027
It was this little girl whom Fantine heard.

38
00:02:24.587 --> 00:02:28.248
Fantine held her breath and listened with a look of joy on her face.

39
00:02:29.352 --> 00:02:30.372
"It's my Cosette!

40
00:02:32.093 --> 00:02:33.393
Oh, how happy we'll be!

41
00:02:34.413 --> 00:02:38.354
She'll chase butterflies in the grass, and I'll teach her the alphabet.

42
00:02:39.255 --> 00:02:40.875
And then when she's older, she'll.

43
00:02:41.715 --> 00:02:45.456
A look of horror crossed Fantine's face as she pointed to something behind the mayor.

44
00:02:45.476 --> 00:02:46.737
"Good grief!

45
00:02:47.097 --> 00:02:48.257
What's the matter, Fantine?"

46
00:02:48.877 --> 00:02:53.919
Madeleine turned and there, leaning against the doorway, stood Javert.

47
00:02:54.779 --> 00:02:59.908
Fantine had not seen the policeman since the day he had arrested her, and she was sure he

48
00:02:59.948 --> 00:03:01.269
had now come for her.

49
00:03:01.289 --> 00:03:05.270
"Mayor Madeleine, save me!"

50
00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:06.370
she screamed.

51
00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:11.012
Jean Valjean, whom Fantine knew as Mayor Madeleine, stood up.

52
00:03:11.832 --> 00:03:15.993
He turned to Fantine and said in his kindest voice, "Calm yourself.

53
00:03:16.813 --> 00:03:18.694
It's not for you that this man comes."

54
00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:23.695
Then Valjean looked steadily at Javert and said, "I know what you want."

55
00:03:23.715 --> 00:03:26.356
"Hurry up," said Javert.

56
00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.761
Fantine looked around in confusion.

57
00:03:29.661 --> 00:03:32.363
There was no one in the room except the mayor and the policeman.

58
00:03:32.903 --> 00:03:36.284
Javert must be talking to her, no matter what the mayor said.

59
00:03:37.065 --> 00:03:42.908
Then she saw something so odd, stranger than anything that had appeared to her when she was delirious

60
00:03:42.928 --> 00:03:43.508
with fever.

61
00:03:44.508 --> 00:03:48.910
She saw Javert seize the mayor by the collar, and the mayor bow his head.

62
00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:50.731
"Mayor Madeleine!"

63
00:03:51.191 --> 00:03:52.816
shouted Fantine.

64
00:03:52.836 --> 00:03:56.779
Javert burst into a horrid laugh, displaying all his teeth.

65
00:04:01.403 --> 00:04:03.625
is no Mayor Madeleine here any longer!"

66
00:04:04.566 --> 00:04:07.448
Valjean did not attempt to loosen Javert's grip on his collar.

67
00:04:07.468 --> 00:04:10.851
"Javert—" "Call me Monsieur Inspector."

68
00:04:10.871 --> 00:04:14.694
"Monsieur, I would like to say something to you in private."

69
00:04:14.714 --> 00:04:16.876
"No, speak now."

70
00:04:16.896 --> 00:04:21.880
"It's a confidential matter, so I'd like—" "What difference does that make to me?"

71
00:04:22.964 --> 00:04:26.767
Valjean turned his head and said, "Give me three days so I can go for the child of

72
00:04:26.807 --> 00:04:29.329
this unfortunate woman and make some arrangements for her!

73
00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.513
I'll pay whatever's necessary, and you can come with me if you want."

74
00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:36.675
He said all this as quickly and quietly as possible.

75
00:04:36.695 --> 00:04:38.617
"Are you making fun of me?"

76
00:04:39.017 --> 00:04:39.758
asked Javert.

77
00:04:39.778 --> 00:04:42.300
"You tell me you're going to get this woman's child?

78
00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:46.203
You might as well come right out and ask me for three days to escape.

79
00:04:46.984 --> 00:04:48.805
Ha-ha! That's a good one!"

80
00:04:48.825 --> 00:04:50.647
"Going for my child?"

81
00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:51.988
Fantine shivered.

82
00:04:52.504 --> 00:04:54.705
"Do you mean she's not here?

83
00:04:55.965 --> 00:04:56.925
Where is Cosette?

84
00:04:57.685 --> 00:04:58.486
Monsieur Mayor!"

85
00:04:59.606 --> 00:05:00.886
Javert stamped his foot.

86
00:05:01.286 --> 00:05:02.067
"Be quiet!

87
00:05:02.547 --> 00:05:07.668
What kind of country is this where convicts are mayors and common criminals are nursed like countesses?

88
00:05:08.488 --> 00:05:11.349
I tell you again there's no Monsieur Mayor here.

89
00:05:12.209 --> 00:05:18.191
There is a robber, a lawbreaker, a convict named Jean Valjean, and I've got him!

90
00:05:18.731 --> 00:05:19.631
That's what there is!"

91
00:05:20.512 --> 00:05:21.812
Fantine started to sit up.

92
00:05:22.248 --> 00:05:24.269
She looked at Valjean, then at Javert.

93
00:05:24.769 --> 00:05:29.452
She opened her mouth as if to speak, and then suddenly sank back upon the pillow with her

94
00:05:29.592 --> 00:05:30.192
eyes closed.

95
00:05:31.353 --> 00:05:36.296
Valjean put his hand over Javert's and pulled the policeman's fingers from his collar.

96
00:05:37.416 --> 00:05:42.079
He quickly checked Fantine's pulse and then whirled back toward Javert.

97
00:05:42.099 --> 00:05:45.021
"You have killed this woman!"

98
00:05:45.041 --> 00:05:47.022
"I don't have time for this.

99
00:05:47.562 --> 00:05:51.124
Come along now before I call the guard downstairs and have him handcuff you."

100
00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:55.287
In the corner of the room there was an old bed with a metal frame.

101
00:05:55.807 --> 00:05:59.030
It was where the nuns rested when they had to watch over a patient at night.

102
00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:03.013
Valjean rushed to the bed and wrenched a metal bar from the frame.

103
00:06:03.453 --> 00:06:06.436
It was an easy thing for a man of his strength to accomplish.

104
00:06:06.456 --> 00:06:12.100
"I advise you not to disturb me now," said Valjean quietly.

105
00:06:13.101 --> 00:06:16.704
Javert stood by the door while Valjean knelt next to Fantine's bed.

106
00:06:17.264 --> 00:06:21.488
He whispered something to her, took her hand, and gently kissed it.

107
00:06:22.272 --> 00:06:26.234
Valjean stood up and said to Javert, "Now I am free to leave with you."

108
00:06:26.835 --> 00:06:29.496
The mayor's arrest produced a sensation in the town.

109
00:06:31.117 --> 00:06:37.701
In less than two hours, his good deeds were forgotten as everyone discussed the convict in their midst.

110
00:06:38.802 --> 00:06:44.385
That night Valjean's housekeeper was thinking sadly about the mayor when he suddenly walked in the door.

111
00:06:44.405 --> 00:06:45.786
"Monsieur Mayor!

112
00:06:45.806 --> 00:06:48.488
I thought you were—" "In jail?

113
00:06:49.172 --> 00:06:52.453
I broke a bar from a window, jumped from a roof, and here I am.

114
00:06:52.993 --> 00:06:54.374
Find Sister Simplice for me.

115
00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.034
It's urgent!"

116
00:06:55.954 --> 00:06:57.234
Valjean went up to his room.

117
00:06:57.755 --> 00:07:01.176
He quickly wrapped up the silver candlesticks and packed them with some other things.

118
00:07:01.196 --> 00:07:04.857
"Do you wish to see Fantine's body one last time?"

119
00:07:05.217 --> 00:07:07.217
asked Sister Simplice when she arrived.

120
00:07:07.237 --> 00:07:10.798
"No, I'm leaving some money here for her burial.

121
00:07:11.278 --> 00:07:12.539
Make sure the priest gets it."

122
00:07:13.459 --> 00:07:16.140
At that moment there was the sound of voices downstairs.

123
00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:21.082
"I swear that no one has come in here all day," said the housekeeper.

124
00:07:21.102 --> 00:07:23.984
"But there's a light upstairs," said Javert.

125
00:07:24.564 --> 00:07:27.166
Valjean blew out his candle and hid behind the door.

126
00:07:28.006 --> 00:07:33.269
When Javert burst through the door, Sister Simplice was kneeling in prayer by the light of one small

127
00:07:33.329 --> 00:07:35.691
candle. Javert hesitated.

128
00:07:36.291 --> 00:07:41.654
He had great respect for authority and especially for the church, so he didn't want to disturb a

129
00:07:41.714 --> 00:07:42.455
nun at prayer.

130
00:07:42.935 --> 00:07:43.335
And yet.

131
00:07:44.396 --> 00:07:48.041
"Sister, Valjean has escaped and we're looking for him.

132
00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:49.802
Have you seen him?"

133
00:07:50.822 --> 00:07:52.483
Sister Simplice raised her eyes.

134
00:07:52.503 --> 00:08:00.706
"No." An hour later a man carrying a bundle walked rapidly out of town, headed in the direction

135
00:08:00.786 --> 00:08:01.386
of Paris.
